  "final_response": "I've completed my contribution to the Clarity Library. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n### Problems Fixed\n- **`framework.md`**: Replaced all `[Title Not Specified]` placeholders with real summaries of each issue's theme, focus, and key insight. Removed the incomplete placeholder section 7 entirely.\n- **`index.md`**: Eliminated the duplicate Issue 06 listing (it appeared under both \"Essays\" and \"Dramatic Works\"), cleaned up all cross-references.\n- **`manifesto.md`**: Fixed broken tool references to point to actual documents.\n\n### New Content Created\n- **`tools_and_templates.md`**: A consolidated field kit — every tool, checklist, and template from across the entire library in one working reference. Includes:\n  - All 6 tools (Filtering Test, Cognitive Load Budget, Dramatist's Cut, Pyramid Structure, Empathy Check, Silence Test)\n  - 3 practical templates (Purpose Statement, Atomic Section Header, Before/After Checklist)\n  - A quick-reference table mapping each issue to its core gift and primary tool\n\n### Updated Navigation\n- **`reading_path.md`**: Added the previously missing Issue 04 to Stage 2; inserted Tools & Templates as a new practical step in Stage 3.\n\nThe library now has no broken references, no duplicate entries, and — crucially — every reader can immediately act on what they've learned rather than just understand it theoretically.",
